<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        2026-09-03 REPOINT (A7 of agent-output/design-checklist-cutover-and-stage-gate.md).

        WAS: actionName/nameSegment TaskFanoutService, entry filter Tasks_Fanned_Out__c = false.
        NOW: actionName/nameSegment ChecklistFanoutService, entry filter
             Checklist_Fanned_Out__c = false.

        THE API NAME OF THIS FLOW IS DELIBERATELY STILL Transaction_Task_Fanout. Every profile in
        force-app/main/default/profiles/ references it by that name (flowAccesses), and the four
        seed/cutover scripts in scripts/ name it in their headers. Renaming the file would break
        all of them for a cosmetic gain. Only the label, the description and the one action element
        were renamed.

        WHY THE SECOND FILTER MOVED TO A DIFFERENT FIELD, AND WHY THAT IS NOT A DETAIL:
        ChecklistFanoutService's own dedupe guard reads Transaction__c.Checklist_Fanned_Out__c
        (ChecklistFanoutService.fanOutChunk). Leaving the entry filter on Tasks_Fanned_Out__c would
        put the flow's guard and the service's guard on two different fields: a deal could enter
        the flow repeatedly and be refused inside, or, after any script that re-arms
        Tasks_Fanned_Out__c, be fanned out TWICE and duplicate the entire checklist. The two flags
        are separate on purpose; see the description on Checklist_Fanned_Out__c.field-meta.xml.

        Tasks_Fanned_Out__c IS NOT READ BY THIS FLOW ANY MORE AND IS NOT CLEARED BY ANYTHING. On
        TXN-0285 it stays true forever as a legacy mutex. Do not "tidy" it to false anywhere:
        writing false to it no longer arms this flow, but TaskFanoutService.fanOutNow still treats
        true as its only dedupe guard, so a false there re-opens the LEGACY fan-out to any other
        caller.

        flowTransactionModel is deliberately still CurrentTransaction. The invocable it now calls
        does not do the work inline; ChecklistFanoutService.fanOut only validates and dedupes the
        request list and issues exactly ONE System.enqueueJob per invocation, handing the 96 rows
        per Transaction to ChecklistFanoutQueueable, which chunks at 50 and chains from its own
        Finalizer. So the synchronous cost charged to the user's save is one enqueue, exactly as it
        was under TaskFanoutService. NewTransaction would buy nothing, would add an async hop in
        front of an already async pipeline, and would move the failure further from the save.

        LEGACY RETIREMENT IS NOT PART OF THIS CHANGE. TaskFanoutService, TaskFanoutQueueable and
        TaskRollupService all remain deployed and callable; they simply have no flow entry point on
        Transaction__c any more. See A8 / M5 of the design.
    -->
    <actionCalls>
        <name>Fan_Out_Checklists</name>
        <label>Fan Out Checklists</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>288</locationY>
        <actionName>ChecklistFanoutService</actionName>
        <actionType>apex</actionType>
        <flowTransactionModel>CurrentTransaction</flowTransactionModel>
        <inputParameters>
            <name>transactionId</name>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </inputParameters>
        <nameSegment>ChecklistFanoutService</nameSegment>
    </actionCalls>
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <description>Day-0 fan-out for Transaction__c. Queues ChecklistFanoutService once a contract execution date exists and the deal has not been claimed by the checklist model. Repointed from TaskFanoutService on 2026-09-03; API name kept for profile and script references.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Transaction Checklist Fanout {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Transaction Checklist Fanout</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Fan_Out_Checklists</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Contract_Executed_Date__c</field>
            <operator>IsNull</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>Checklist_Fanned_Out__c</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <object>Transaction__c</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
